  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mekong-Australia Partnership - Vietnam Climate Change Adaptation Programs</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This investment aims to promote the use of improved rice farming technology by private sector rice companies in the Mekong Delta. The uptake of new farming practices and technology is expected to reduce emissions, increase yields, and reduce water usage in approximately 200,000 hectares of rice farming via this investment. It is an example of how Australia is delivering on the Joint Statement on Commitment to Practical Climate Action made by the Prime Ministers of Australia and Vietnam at COP26. It also demonstrates how Australia uses the development program to promote private sector growth.</narrative>
  </description>
